preConditionHook:
// EEC E16's serial-correlation gate: wait X bars after a winner, Y after a
// loser, and let the backtest's first trade through. All three accessors are
// measured (the `positionprofit(n)`/`totaltrades` register row,
// EL_PositionProfit_Probe.txt): PositionProfit(1) is the most recently
// CLOSED position net of the full round turn (0.0 before any close),
// BarsSinceExit is 0 on the exit's fill bar, and TotalTrades is already
// incremented at that bar's close. EL evaluates the whole OR every bar
// (no short-circuit), but every term here is a stateless accessor read, so
// C++ short-circuiting cannot diverge. A signal-time gate: it also holds
// back reversals, exactly as the book's EL does.
cooldownOver =
    (el_gt(ctx.PositionProfit(1), 0.0) &&
     el_ge((double)ctx.BarsSinceExit(), waitAfterWin)) ||
    (el_le(ctx.PositionProfit(1), 0.0) &&
     el_ge((double)ctx.BarsSinceExit(), waitAfterLoss)) ||
    ctx.TotalTrades() == 0;
